  "text": " So, what do you do? I was at a cafe. Normal question. Apparently, I needed a lawyer. I said, I work on a computer, so does the person fixing the card machine? We had narrowed it down to electricity. They asked what kind of work. I said, creative stuff. Creative stuff? Excellent. Now I sounded like I sold suspicious candles. I could have just said animator. At home, I'll explain a three-frame blink like I'm defending a thesis. In public? Computer activities. Then they asked to see something. My phone suddenly felt like it contained every bad hand I'd ever drawn. I opened a video, then immediately started explaining why the old drawings didn't count. The hair was wrong. The timing was weird. I was giving a guided tour of the emergency exits before they'd even watched it. They laughed at the little joke. Not at me. At the part I'd spent an entire evening trying to make funny. Then came the terrifying follow-up. You made that? I almost said, sort of. As if the drawings had wandered in by themselves. But I said, yeah, I make animated stories. My voice did that tiny wobble. The cafe continued operating. Nobody asked for a certificate. They just wanted to see the next bit. I was the only one making me audition. So, next time someone asks, I'm an animator. Still learning, still redrawing hands. Apparently, I'm allowed to say it before I'm finished.",
